Example here: https://github.com/urbanairship/terraform-infrastructure/pull/276.

Added the logic to handle different RF versions in atest. It's more flexible than old solution (the old one used "_rf3" style suffixes in the file name to determine version). In the new framework it's possible to set target version. Example:

```
class TestRule(RuleAcceptance):
    def test_rule(self):
        self.check_rule(expected_file="expected_output.txt", target_version=">=5.0")

    def test_rule_rf3(self):
        self.check_rule(expected_file="expected_output_rf4.txt", target_version="==4.1.3")

    def test_rule_rf4(self):
        self.check_rule(expected_file="expected_output_rf3.txt", target_version="==3.2.2")
```

It can match particular version or range of versions.
